    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nDNG Martin O'Connor Estate Agents are delighted to present for sale this attractive two-bedroom semi-detached bungalow, ideally situated within the established Racecourse Hill development in the heart of Clifden, Co. Galway. Occupying a convenient position within this mature residential setting of just twelve homes, No. 12 offers an excellent opportunity for first-time buyers, those looking to downsize, or investors seeking a property in one of Connemara's most sought-after towns.Extending to approximately 62 sq.m. (667 sq.ft.), the property offers comfortable single-storey accommodation with a practical layout designed for everyday living. The home benefits from front and rear gardens together with valuable off-street parking and presents an excellent opportunity for a purchaser to modernise and personalise to their own style and requirements.Racecourse Hill enjoys an exceptionally convenient location just a short stroll from Clifden town centre, where a wide range of amenities are on your doorstep, including supermarkets, cafés, restaurants, shops, schools, medical facilities and leisure amenities. Renowned as the capital of Connemara, Clifden offers an unrivalled lifestyle surrounded by the spectacular scenery of the Wild Atlantic Way, with beautiful beaches, scenic walking routes, cycling trails and Connemara National Park all within easy reach.Whether you are seeking a permanent home, a holiday retreat or an investment property, No. 12 Racecourse Hill represents a wonderful opportunity to acquire a home in a well-established residential location with every convenience close at hand.The property enjoys a front garden with off-street parking together with a private rear garden, providing a pleasant outdoor space with excellent potential for gardening, entertaining or simply relaxing. The mature surroundings of Racecourse Hill create a peaceful residential environment while remaining just minutes from the vibrant centre of Clifden.Early viewing is highly recommended to fully appreciate all that this ideally located home has to offer. For further details or to arrange a viewing, contact the sole selling agents, DNG Martin O'Connor Estate Agents, on 091 866708."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nEntrance Hall - \nA welcoming entrance hall with laminate wood flooring, providing access to the main living accommodation.\n\nLiving Room - \nA comfortable living room with wooden flooring and provision for an open fireplace.\n\nKitchen - \nThe kitchen is fitted with a range of floor and wall units and includes an electric hob and oven. Tiled flooring and plumbing for a dishwasher complete this practical space.\n\nBedroom 1 - \nA double bedroom with wooden flooring and built-in wardrobes, overlooking the rear garden with views towards Clifden Town.\n\nBedroom 2 - \nA spacious double bedroom with wooden flooring and built-in wardrobes. French patio doors provide direct access to the patio and enjoy views towards Clifden Town.\n\nBathroom - \nA fully tiled bathroom fitted with a bath with overhead shower, wash hand basin and WC.\n\nUtility Room - \nA useful utility room plumbed for a washing machine and dryer, with a hot press located alongside.\n\n"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "<ul><li> Attractive two-bedroom semi-detached bungalow.</li><li> Approx. 62 sq.m (667 sq.ft.) of accommodation.</li><li> Situated within the established Racecourse Hill development.</li><li> Mature residential setting comprising just 12 homes.</li><li> Front and private rear gardens.</li><li> Off-street parking.</li><li> Comfortable single-storey living.</li><li> Excellent opportunity to modernise and add value.</li><li> Short walk to Clifden town centre and all local amenities.</li><li> Ideal for first-time buyers, downsizers, holiday home purchasers or investors.</li><li> OFCH</ul>"
      },
